{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (#5399) from a work queue in the go-unix-utils project. The task is to implement srd057-mv requirements R3.1-R3.3 (output control and target directory) for the `cmd/mv` utility. Specifically:\n   - R3.1: `-v`/`--verbose` flag to print file move operations in format 'SOURCE -> DEST' or 'renamed SOURCE -> DEST'\n   - R3.2: `-t DIRECTORY`/`--target-directory=DIRECTORY` to move all SOURCE arguments into DIRECTORY\n   - R3.3: `-T`/`--no-target-directory` to treat DEST as a normal file, not a directory\n   \n   The task specifies modifying `cmd/mv/main.go` and `cmd/mv/mv_test.go`, running differential tests against `gmv` reference binary, and verifying all acceptance criteria (AC1-AC5).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing Go binary output against GNU reference binary (`gmv`)\n   - SIGPIPE handler installation via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Custom test harness with `runMvTest`/`runMvTestInput` helpers that set up isolated temp directories for both Go and reference binaries\n   - Normalizers for stderr comparison (binary name normalization, case normalization, \"try\" line filtering)\n   - `overwriteMode` enum using iota for interactive/force/no-clobber modes\n   - Cross-device move handling (copy + delete fallback when `os.Rename` returns `EXDEV`)\n   - Go module at `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils`\n   - Git is managed externally by the orchestrator - NO git commands allowed\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd057-mv.yaml`\n     - Source of truth for R3.1-R3.3 requirements\n     - R3.1: verbose output format 'SOURCE -> DEST' or 'renamed SOURCE